<title>USA: U.S. cattle on feed - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. cattle on feed - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA U.S. cattle on feed. 7 states, 1,000-plus head feedlots (data in 1,000 head):</p>
<p>    -			Pct----1996-----1995     1994</p>
<p> On Feed December 1    103   8,973    8,685    8,198</p>
<p> During November:	Pct----1996-----1995     1994</p>
<p> -Placed on Feed	 108   1,943    1,804    1,642</p>
<p> -Marketed		  97   1,438    1,478    1,370</p>
<p> -Other Disappearance  108	66	 61	 62</p>
<p> On Feed November 1    101   8,534-R  8,420    7,988</p>
<p> -			   Pct---Dec 1----Nov 1</p>
<p>  U.S. On Feed	   105  10,598   10,073-R</p>
<p>USDA revised the November number of cattle on feed on large lots to 8.534 million head from the previously reported 8.544 million. It also revised November 1 U.S. total cattle on feed to 10.073 million head from 10.070 million.</p>
<p>Analysts on average had expected the number of cattle on feed in the seven key states on December 1 at 103.2 percent of a year ago, and November placements at 105 percent of a year ago.</p>
<p>The seven major states are Arizona, California, Colorado, Iowa, Kansas, Nebraska and Texas.</p>
